We want to minimize $D^2$ subject to the constraint $3x - 4y + 5z = 30$.
We can use the method of Lagrange multipliers. Let $g(x, y, z) = 3x - 4y + 5z - 30$. Then we have the following equations:
\begin{align*} \label{eq:1} \frac{\partial D^2}{\partial x} &= \lambda \frac{\partial g}{\partial x} \\ \frac{\partial D^2}{\partial y} &= \lambda \frac{\partial g}{\partial y} \\ \frac{\partial D^2}{\partial z} &= \lambda \frac{\partial g}{\partial z} \\ 3x - 4y + 5z &= 30 \end{align*}
