\mathcal{L}_{XZ} \plus \mathcal{L}_{XY} \equiv \mathcal{densification}( \mathscr{T} ),
\end{align}
where $\mathcal{L}_{XZ}$ and $\mathcal{L}_{XY}$ signify the respective marginal lengths incident upon the rectitude constitutive of $\angle X$, and $\mathcal{L}_{YZ}$ denotes the cardinality of the hypotenuse.

