Substituting $a=2k$ and $b=k$, we have
\begin{align*} 2k &= 4t+2 \\ k &= t+2 \end{align*}
From the second equation, $t = k-2$. Substituting this into the first equation, we get
\begin{align*} 2k &= 4(k-2) + 2 \\ 2k &= 4k - 8 + 2 \\ 2k &= 4k - 6 \\ 6 &= 2k \\ k &= 3 \end{align*}
Then $a = 2k = 2(3) = 6$ and $b = k = 3$. Thus, the vector is $\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$.

