\begin{align*} (x + 5)(2x - 1) &= x(2x) + x(-1) + 5(2x) + 5(-1) \\ &= 2x^2 - x + 10x - 5 \\ &= 2x^2 + 9x - 5 \end{align*}
Thus,
\begin{align*} (2x - 5)(x + 7) - (x + 5)(2x - 1) &= (2x^2 + 9x - 35) - (2x^2 + 9x - 5) \\ &= 2x^2 + 9x - 35 - 2x^2 - 9x + 5 \\ &= (2x^2 - 2x^2) + (9x - 9x) + (-35 + 5) \\ &= 0 + 0 - 30 \\ &= -30 \end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{-30}$

