Let $u = \begin{pmatrix} \cos \alpha & \sin \alpha \end{pmatrix}$ and $v = \begin{pmatrix} \cos \beta & \sin \beta \end{pmatrix}.$  Then we seek to minimize
\begin{align*} &\| \mathcal{A} u + \mathcal{B} v - \mathcal{C} \|^2 \\ &= (2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)^2 + (3 \sin \alpha + 4 \cos \beta - 15)^2 \end{align*}
where $\mathcal{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 0 & 5 \end{pmatrix},$ $\mathcal{B} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & 5 \\ 2 & 0 \end{pmatrix},$ and $\mathcal{C} = \begin{pmatrix} 8 \\ 15 \end{pmatrix}.$

Let $f(\alpha, \beta) = (2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)^2 + (2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15)^2.$  We have
\begin{align*} f(\alpha, \beta) &= (2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)^2 + (2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15)^2 \\ &= (2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)^2 + (2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15)^2. \end{align*}To minimize $f(\alpha, \beta),$ we take the partial derivatives with respect to $\alpha$ and $\beta,$ and set them to 0:
\begin{align*} \frac{\partial f}{\partial \alpha} &= 2(2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)(-2 \sin \alpha) + 2(2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15)(2 \cos \alpha) = 0 \\ &\implies (2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)(-\sin \alpha) + (2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15) \cos \alpha = 0 \\ &\implies -2 \cos \alpha \sin \alpha - 5 \sin \beta \sin \alpha + 8 \sin \alpha + 2 \sin \alpha \cos \alpha + 5 \cos \beta \cos \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha = 0 \\ &\implies -5 \sin \beta \sin \alpha + 8 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta \cos \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha = 0 \\ &\implies 8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha = 5 (\sin \beta \sin \alpha - \cos \beta \cos \alpha) \\ &\implies 8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha = -5 \cos (\alpha + \beta) \end{align*}
\begin{align*} \frac{\partial f}{\partial \beta} &= 2(2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)(5 \cos \beta) + 2(2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15)(-5 \sin \beta) = 0 \\ &\implies (2 \cos \alpha + 5 \sin \beta - 8)(5 \cos \beta) - (2 \sin \alpha + 5 \cos \beta - 15)(5 \sin \beta) = 0 \\ &\implies 10 \cos \alpha \cos \beta + 25 \sin \beta \cos \beta - 40 \cos \beta - 10 \sin \alpha \sin \beta - 25 \cos \beta \sin \beta + 75 \sin \beta = 0 \\ &\implies 10 \cos \alpha \cos \beta - 10 \sin \alpha \sin \beta - 40 \cos \beta + 75 \sin \beta = 0 \\ &\implies \cos \alpha \cos \beta - \sin \alpha \sin \beta - 4 \cos \beta + 7.5 \sin \beta = 0 \\ &\implies \cos (\alpha + \beta) - 4 \cos \beta + 7.5 \sin \beta = 0 \end{align*}
We have
\begin{align*} 8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha &= -5 \cos (\alpha + \beta) \\ \cos (\alpha + \beta) &= \cos \alpha \cos \beta - \sin \alpha \sin \beta - 4 \cos \beta + 7.5 \sin \beta \end{align*}
Let $\alpha = \pi$ and $\beta = 0.$ Then
\begin{align*} 8 \sin \pi - 15 \cos \pi &= -5 \cos (\pi + 0) \\ -15(-1) &= -5(-1) \\ 15 &= 5 \end{align*}This doesn't work.
Let $\alpha = 0$ and $\beta = \pi.$ Then
\begin{align*} 8 \sin 0 - 15 \cos 0 &= -5 \cos (0 + \pi) \\ -15 &= -5(-1) \\ -15 &= 5 \end{align*}This doesn't work.

Consider the case where $\alpha = \beta.$  Then
\begin{align*} 8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha &= -5 \cos (2 \alpha) \\ \cos (2 \alpha) &= \cos^2 \alpha - \sin^2 \alpha = 2 \cos^2 \alpha - 1 = 1 - 2 \sin^2 \alpha \end{align*}Thus,
\begin{align*} 8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha &= -5 (2 \cos^2 \alpha - 1) = -10 \cos^2 \alpha + 5 \\ 8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha &= -5 (1 - 2 \sin^2 \alpha) = -5 + 10 \sin^2 \alpha \end{align*}
We want to find $\alpha$ such that $8 \sin \alpha - 15 \cos \alpha = -5 \cos (\alpha + \beta)$ and $\cos (\alpha + \beta) - 4 \cos \beta + 7.5 \sin \beta = 0.$

Taking $\alpha = \beta = 0,$ we have
\begin{align*} f(0, 0) &= (2 \cos 0 + 5 \sin 0 - 8)^2 + (2 \sin 0 + 5 \cos 0 - 15)^2 \\ &= (2 - 8)^2 + (5 - 15)^2 \\ &= (-6)^2 + (-10)^2 = 36 + 100 = 136 \end{align*}
Taking $\alpha = \beta = \frac{\pi}{2},$ we have
\begin{align*} f(\frac{\pi}{2}, \frac{\pi}{2}) &= (2 \cos \frac{\pi}{2} + 5 \sin \frac{\pi}{2} - 8)^2 + (2 \sin \frac{\pi}{2} + 5 \cos \frac{\pi}{2} - 15)^2 \\ &= (0 + 5 - 8)^2 + (2 + 0 - 15)^2 \\ &= (-3)^2 + (-13)^2 = 9 + 169 = 178 \end{align*}
Let $\alpha = \frac{\pi}{2}$ and $\beta = 0.$  Then
\begin{align*} f(\frac{\pi}{2}, 0) &= (2 \cos \frac{\pi}{2} + 5 \sin 0 - 8)^2 + (2 \sin \frac{\pi}{2} + 5 \cos 0 - 15)^2 \\ &= (0 + 0 - 8)^2 + (2 + 5 - 15)^2 \\ &= (-8)^2 + (-8)^2 = 64 + 64 = 128 \end{align*}
