Evaluate \begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c
\end{align*} when $c=3$.

response:
Let $f(x) = \left(x^{x} - x \cdot (x-1)^{x} \right)^{x}$. The problem mandates the evaluation of $f(x)$ at $x = 3$.
Thus, we are requested to compute
\begin{align*}
\label{eq:1}
\left(3^{3} - 3 \cdot (3-1)^{3} \right)^{3}
\end{align}
induced by the predicate $c \in \mathbb{R}^{+}$.

The requisite constitutive stipulations necessitate the progressive resolution of the ensuing cascade.
Firstly, the exponentiated transduction of the monadic operator furnishes
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{a} \coloneqq 3^3 = 3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3 = 27.
\end{align*}
Secondly, the monadic quantification predicated upon the antecedent furnishes
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{b} \coloneqq 3-1 = 2.
\end{align*}
Subsequently, the exponentiation of $\mathfrak{b}$ yields
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{c} \coloneqq 2^3 = 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 = 8.
\end{align*}
Thus, $3(2^3) = 3(8) = 24$.
Hence, the term within the parentheses reduces to
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{d} \coloneqq 27 - 24 = 3.
\end{align*}
Lastly, the cubing of $\mathfrak{d}$ furnishes
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{e} \coloneqq 3^3 = 3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3 = 27.
\end{align*}

Thus,
\begin{align*}
\left(c^c-c(c-1)^c\right)^c &= \left(3^3 - 3(3-1)^3\right)^3 \\
&= \left(27 - 3(2^3)\right)^3 \\
&= (27 - 3(8))^3 \\
&= (27 - 24)^3 \\
&= 3^3 \\
&= 27
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $\boxed{27}$

