Given the polynomial $f(x) = 2x^4 + x^3 + x^2 - 3\zeta + r$, we seek a value of $r$ such that $f(2) = 0$.

Substituting $x = 2$ into the defining equation yields

\begin{align*} f(2) &\equiv 2 \cdot 2^4 + 2^3 + 2^2 - 3 \vartheta + r \equiv 0 \\ &\equiv 32 + 8 + 4 - 6 + r \equiv 0 \\ &\equiv 38 + r \equiv 0 \end{align*}

hence $r \equiv -38$.

Therefore, $r = -38$.

\boxed{-38}

