\begin{align*} \mathcal{D} &:= \begin{vmatrix} \sin^2 A & \operatorname{cotangens} A & 1 \\ \sin^2 B & \operatorname{cotangens} B & 1 \\ \sin^2 C & \operatorname{cotangens} C & 1 \end{align}
in conjunction with the constraint $A+B+C \equiv \pi$ \textit{ante}.

Permuting the columns yields
\begin{align*} \mathcal{D} &:= \begin{vmatrix} \sin^2 \xi & \mathcal{O} \mathfrak{f} \xi & 1 \\ \sin^2 \vartheta & \mathcal{O} \mathfrak{f} \vartheta & 1 \\ \sin^2 \chi & \mathcal{O} \mathfrak{f} \chi & 1 \end{vmatrix} \end{align}
where $\xi$, $\vartheta$, $\chi$ are $A$, $B$, $C$ in some permutation.

Expanding the determinant along the third column, we obtain
\begin{align*} \begin{vmatrix} \sin^2 A & \cot A & 1 \\ \sin^2 B & \cot B & 1 \\ \sin^2 C & \cot C & 1 \end{vmatrix} &= \begin{vmatrix} \sin^2 B & \cot B \\ \sin^2 C & \cot C \end{vmatrix} - \begin{vmatrix} \sin^2 A & \cot A \\ \sin^2 C & \cot C \end{vmatrix} + \begin{vmatrix} \sin^2 A & \cot A \\ \sin^2 B & \cot B \end{vmatrix} \\ &= (\sin^2 B \cot C - \sin^2 C \cot B) - (\sin^2 A \cot C - \sin^2 C \cot A) + (\sin^2 A \cot B - \sin^2 B \cot A) \\ &= \sin^2 B \frac{\cos C}{\sin C} - \sin^2 C \frac{\cos B}{\sin B} - \sin^2 A \frac{\cos C}{\sin C} + \sin^2 C \frac{\cos A}{\sin C} + \sin^2 A \frac{\cos B}{\sin A} - \sin^2 B \frac{\cos A}{\sin B} \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 B \cos C}{\sin C} - \frac{\sin^2 C \cos B}{\sin B} - \frac{\sin^2 A \cos C}{\sin C} + \frac{\sin^2 C \cos A}{\sin C} + \frac{\sin^2 A \cos B}{\sin A} - \frac{\sin^2 B \cos A}{\sin B} \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 B \cos C - \sin^2 C \cos B}{\sin C} - \frac{\sin^2 A \cos C - \sin^2 C \cos A}{\sin C} + \frac{\sin^2 A \cos B - \sin^2 B \cos A}{\sin A} \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 B \cos C - \sin^2 C \cos B}{\sin C} - \frac{\sin^2 A \cos C - \sin^2 C \cos A}{\sin C} + \frac{\sin^2 A \cos B - \sin^2 B \cos A}{\sin A} \end{align*}
Since $A+B+C = \pi,$ $C = \pi - (A+B),$ so $\sin C = \sin (A+B)$ and $\cos C = -\cos (A+B).$  Then
\begin{align*} \sin^2 B \cos C - \sin^2 C \cos B &= \sin^2 B (-\cos (A+B)) - \sin^2 (\pi - (A+B)) \cos B \\ &= -\sin^2 B \cos (A+B) - \sin^2 (A+B) \cos B \end{align*}
Also,
\begin{align*} \sin^2 A \cos C - \sin^2 C \cos A &= \sin^2 A (-\cos (A+B)) - \sin^2 (\pi - (A+B)) \cos A \\ &= -\sin^2 A \cos (A+B) - \sin^2 (A+B) \cos A \end{align*}
We have
\begin{align*} \sin^2 B \cot C - \sin^2 C \cot B &= \sin^2 B \frac{\cos C}{\sin C} - \sin^2 C \frac{\cos B}{\sin B} \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 B \cos C \sin B - \sin^2 C \cos B \sin C}{\sin B \sin C} \\ &= \frac{\sin^3 B \cos C - \sin^3 C \cos B}{\sin B \sin C} \end{align*}
We have
\begin{align*} \sin^2 A \cot C - \sin^2 C \cot A &= \sin^2 A \frac{\cos C}{\sin C} - \sin^2 C \frac{\cos A}{\sin A} \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 A \cos C \sin A - \sin^2 C \cos A \sin C}{\sin A \sin C} \\ &= \frac{\sin^3 A \cos C - \sin^3 C \cos A}{\sin A \sin C} \end{align*}
We have
\begin{align*} \sin^2 B \cot A - \sin^2 A \cot B &= \sin^2 B \frac{\cos A}{\sin A} - \sin^2 A \frac{\cos B}{\sin B} \\ &= \frac{\sin^2 B \cos A \sin B - \sin^2 A \cos B \sin A}{\sin A \sin B} \\ &= \frac{\sin^3 B \cos A - \sin^3 A \cos B}{\sin A \sin B} \end{align*}
The determinant is 0.

