\begin{align*} \cos \left( -300^\circ \right) \Longleftrightarrow \cos \left( 360^\circ - 300^\circ \right) \Longleftrightarrow \cos \left( 60^\circ \right) \end{align*}
and therefore
\begin{align*} \sec \left( -300^\circ \right) \equiv \frac{1}{\cos \left( 60^\circ \right)} \equiv \frac{1}{1/2} \equiv 2 \end{align*}

